...What had Granny Ichihime said?

The Owari Tokugawa&#x27;s guarded school. Kan-ryuu, considered such a supreme art of the spear that they kept it inside one domain for two hundred years. To stop that spearpoint with a sword...

If I remembered correctly—

&#x27;Countermeasure? Hmm. Let me see.&#x27;

&#x27;Dodging won&#x27;t let you dodge it. Block, and you only get knocked away.&#x27;

&#x27;No. Nothing. Not happening.&#x27;

My voice in the memory answered those irresponsible words. Now I was saying the same thing again.

And Granny, that monument to irresponsibility, shrugged in my memory, looking faintly amused.

&#x27;Arre, a sword won&#x27;t do anything. If winning is so compulsory for you, bring a pistol or something, no?&#x27;
